# Frontend Auth

## Session

- HttpOnly cookie set by the API (no token in `sessionStorage`)
- `httpClient` uses `credentials: 'include'`
- Client fetches `/api/v1/auth/csrf` and sends `X-CSRF-TOKEN` on mutations
- Prefer `VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1` through the Vite/nginx same-origin proxy

## Stores

`stores/auth.ts` owns login, logout, profile, password changes, roles, permissions, and hydration through `/auth/me`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
await authApi.login({ email, password })
await auth.hydrate() // on boot in main.ts
```

## Router guards

```typescript
meta: { requiresAuth: true }           // redirect to login
meta: { guest: true }                   // redirect authenticated users away
meta: { permission: 'users.manage' }    // global permission
```

## Views

- `LoginView`, `ProfileView`, and `ChangePasswordView` call `useAuthStore()`
- Show `auth.error`; disable submit while `auth.loading`
- Users with `mustChangePassword` may only access the password-change/logout flow
- There is no public registration view
